ufficiency or elevated sweat chloride", "Inborn Error of Metabolism: insufficient evidence for multisystem involvement beyond respiratory/cardiac", "Acquired Bronchiectasis: less likely given birth-onset pattern and possible familial component"], "alarm_features": ["Persistent sinus and respiratory symptoms since birth", "Airway dilation on imaging", "Cardiac anomaly (tricuspid stenosis)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Primary Ciliary Dyskinesia and Related Ciliary Disorders", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.4669260700389105, "danger": 0.2, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["MRI airway dilation is more consistent with structural/developmental causes (e.g., ciliary dysfunction in B1) than inflammatory pulmonary disease (B3), moderat…"], "evidence_against": ["The absence of sweat chloride elevation or heterotaxy weakens primary ciliary dyskinesia (B1) but does not exclude it, as these findings may not always be pres…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.3, "interrupt_relevance": 0.1, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "etiology", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Congenital Cardiac Syndromes with Cardiopulmonary and Growth Impairment", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.45826513911620287, "posterior": 0.36316472114137477, "danger": 0.1, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Tricuspid stenosis and persistent growth impairment provide weak support for congenital cardiac syndromes (B2), though normal growth progression reported by gu…"], "evidence_against": ["Normal growth and bowel function reported by guardians provide weak evidence against congenital cardiac syndromes (B2), which typically present with more sever…"], "unresolved